        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/df788c/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-20T16:56:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>some few questions about mobility...</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>yesterday we were playing legacy and tachyon vs. Baron Blade. We discussed a lot about mobility (both tachyon and legacy). You can see legacy flying around megalopolis at level 20 (yes....high very high) to avoid being punished by Blade inventions and soldiers but Tachyon is simply jumping around following the level of each building... so in plain rules lenguage, we decided to let Legacy avoid triggering hazard spaces since he is flying, but Tachyon not unless she was using her special power that let her pass without triggering hazard spaces. Think this is not following the rules but will be verty tematic...what you guys think?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>another question hazzard spaces trigger inmediately &nbsp;if the entrance was in the last movemet? or in this instance you have to wait until the to be continued phase to activate them?</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:42:44.463Z",
