      {
        "id": 119634,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-10-21T12:27:20.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"jac\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/df788c/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> jac:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I was using the flying smash…well…the plan was to fly high and land in a central space in which i could potentially finish 3 different blade inventions…flying was the only way to get there witout triggering the spaces since mobility let you move without taking into account changes in elevetion, meaning Legacy can move from elevation 20 to floor without any problem…o so we thought… <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=12\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sounds like you're assuming they can't shoot up?  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/smiling_imp.png?v=12\" title=\":smiling_imp:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":smiling_imp:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>\n<p>These are the kinds of unbalancing things and open questions that will come up with home rules like this. It can be thematically fun, but it makes the game more complex, opens all kinds of questions, etc. Because it's not cooperative, you'll have to make sure everyone is on the same page as to how things should work, unless your gaming group is just really big on theme and not as big on competition.  <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=12\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"></p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:52:53.965Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
